WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.080
Today we step into the Russian woods to unlock animal names that will have your vocabulary growing with confidence. I'm Olya, and this is Привет, Русский, episode 74. Our word of the day is Lisa. Lisa. Lisa. It means fox. Imagine a Lisa fox, leaping like a slide-little acrobat. The sound even feels quick and clever. Lisa. Repeat after me. Lisa. Now, listen again at normal speed. Lisa. We can say Lisa маленькая.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.820
Это means the fox is small.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.900
The Russian woods are full of animals, and we will learn their names today.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.460
Next comes tigger.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.320
Tigger.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.160
Tigger.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.360
It means tiger.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.940
Tiger roars just like the English tiger.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.200
Easy to remember.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.420
Tiger, большой.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:45.780
The tiger is big.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.040
Repeat after me.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:47.760
Tiger.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.280
Now at normal speed.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:50.020
Tigger.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.440
Slone comes next.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.280
Slone.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.040
Slone.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.240
It means elephant.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.780
Think of a slow, strong elephant, strolling when you hear slone.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.180
Слон есть, да эльфант Иц. Репит авторми. Слон.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.060
Лев фолос. Лев. Лев.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.180
Ит Минс Лайн. Лев, Саунс Лек Лев, ботводокингов до джангел.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.340
Лев спит, да Лайн слепс. Репит авторми. Лев.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:18.840
Змея из доснейк. Змея, змея. Змея хисософтлилека с лидер.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.400
Змея ползает. Доснейк кролс. Репит авторми. Змея.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.000
Лягушка Минс Фрок. Лягушка. Лягушка.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.760
Итлипс деслека фрога на понд, Лягушка прыгает, дофрог джампс, репита в торми, лягушка.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:43.280
Мышь из дымаус, Мышь, Мышь из Квыконтайнии, Лека-маус Дартинговей, Мышь маленькая, дымауса смол, репита в торми, Мышь.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:54.520
Обезьяна минзманки, А обезьяна, Обезьяна, Итсвингс from 3-3 в из-энергии, Обезьяна играет, Дыманки-плейс, репита в торми, Обезьяна.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.560
А now that you know this animal names, we can put them to work in sentences.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.000
Russian warps change a little depending on who does the action.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.580
Take the sub-yea-gaat.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:04.980
That means the fox runs.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.540
Tiger speed means the tiger sleeps.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.060
Sloan yes, means the elephant eats.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:14.020
The warp ending shows the subject without extra wars like he or she.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.020
You can now say simple things about which animal does.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.260
There's something really cool about one of today's warps that takes us on a quick

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.100
journey through time.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:27.820
Тигр started an ancient Persian as tigra, meaning arrow because of the tiger swift stripes.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.860
It traveled through Greek and Latin before reaching Russian in the 18th century.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:39.240
The world looks almost exactly like the English tiger, yet watch out because the same sound can mean something else in other languages.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.720
Picture a tiger shooting forward like an arrow, and that Persian image helps the sound stick.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:49.420
In Russian fairy tales, the clever Lisa often outsmarts bigger animals.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.940
Стори с лак до фокси и крейн, течь children that brains can beat size.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.140
Kids grow up with the stales, and the lesson stays with them.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.760
Remember poisede from a few lessons ago?

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.220
Poised means train.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.500
Now imagine animals riding one.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.380
Do you remember what Lisa means?

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.180
Try using Lisa бегает 3 times today.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.460
For kids, draw your favorite animal from our list, and say its name out loud while you color.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.920
For adults, look at an animal picture and make a sentence like tiger большой.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.900
Молодец, повторите сегодняшние слова один раз в слух, и они ваши.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.400
Расскажите о нашем шоу другу, который тоже учит русский.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.480
До встречи.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.080
Пока!

